---
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>Daily Sheet prototype review</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-xl px-5 py-8">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Daily Sheet prototype</h1>
      <p class="mt-3">One design, with complete menus and an independent source-failure scenario. Data is a fixed research snapshot from 22 October 2026. Sindhi uses Menu 1, as requested.</p>
      <nav aria-label="Prototype review scenarios" class="mt-6 grid border-t border-ink divide-y divide-rule">
        <a class="py-4 underline" href="/lunch/">Lunch · all three menus</a>
        <a class="py-4 underline" href="/dinner/">Dinner · all three menus</a>
        <a class="py-4 underline" href="/lunch/?scenario=mixed">Failure example · FC1 saved, FC2 missing, Sindhi available</a>
      </nav>
      <p class="mt-6">Try scrolling to Sindhi, then changing meals using the sticky switcher. The comparison returns to the beginning. Jump links scroll the same document; all menus remain open.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-secondary">The failure example is simulated. This local prototype has no live menu ingestion or infrastructure.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
